Category: IT Services Location: Fort Western Province Sri Lanka We are urgently looking for a REMOTE Senior DevOps Engineer - .NET/AWS for an international organization in New York. Candidates need to be fluent in English. All positions are long-term. This position is open for freelancers and employees.
Candidates need to be able to work 2-3 hours per day in the normal office hours of New York, US. (Example 9 AM NY time equals 7:30 PM.)
The applicant should be an experienced hands-on DevOps Engineer with a history of working in an agile environment. Candidates must have proficiency and hands-on experience in DevOps in CI/CD technologies, AWS services, and GitLab.

Tasks and deliverables

Work with an agile team to implement deployment automation for .NET and Angular related project;

Setup GitLab Project as per the needs and standard practices of the Organization;

Setup required infrastructure for as-is migration of a project from On-Prem to AWS;

Implement the CI/CD pipelines with GitLab or AWS;

Automation of code builds and deployments incorporating automated QA gates;

Implement process tracking and monitoring application performance in AWS cloud environment and on-premise data centers;

Develop a proof of concepts and prototypes for the above processes to match industry standards;

Profile

Proven track record working in an agile remote team with task-based deliveries

8+ years of experience in scripting languages: Python, Shell, and PowerShell;

5+ years of experience on Terraform and AWS CloudFormation;

5+ years of handling and setting up projects on GitLab, Git Runner with at least 3+ years in maintaining .NET related projects;

5+ years of hands-on experience in Continuous Integration/Continuous Delivery automation on GitLab and AWS;

Experience in AWS Systems Manager (SSM);

Experience in administering Windows operating systems;

Experience in AWS services IAM, EC2, S3, CloudFront, ECS, KMS, Secret Manager, Cognito;

Experience in Lambda, GitLab Runner, AWS CI/CD pipeline services, YAML, JSON, and XML;

Experience following agile methodologies such as SCRUM or Kanban desired;

Familiar with various git branching strategies pull request concepts;

Knowledge/experience working in hybrid cloud environments such as AWS and on-premise data centers e.g with Azure service fabric and Docker containers;

English language proficiency (oral and written);

Offered

A challenging role for an international organization in New York;

Expérience : Tu justifies de 4 ans minimum d’expérience sur un rôle similaire (MLOps, ML engineer, OPS Engineer, Platform Engineer);
Pédagogie et Sens du service : Tu sais accompagner les utilisateurs avec clarté, traduire des concepts IA complexes en solutions techniques simples, et rédiger une documentation robuste;
Curiosité : La veille technologique fait partie de ton ADN;
Esprit collaboratif : Tu t'épanouis dans un environnement agile où le partage est la règle;
Communication : Un excellent relationnel pour fédérer autour de tes solutions. Ton anglais est fluide pour évoluer dans notre contexte international.

Organisation de travail hybride ;
Matériel fourni en accord avec tes missions et nos engagements sociétaux (Mac ou Windows) ;
Une équipe de projet locale au sein d'un réseau mondial (possibilité de carrière internationale) ;
Développement des compétences et accompagnement (diversité des projets, certifications techniques dès la première année, formations internes et externes, etc.) ;
Package de rémunération (participation des employés aux actions de l'entreprise, bonus mensuels/trimestriels).
